multiplication rule for dependent and independent events

dependent events= events that affect the probability of each other.

for example: probability of getting one king without putting it back in the deck is = 4/52 as total 4 kings in deck

            then getting probability of queen after getting one king will be affected as = 4/51 as one king is already taken

            then pr(k and queen)= pr(king) * pr(queen)/pr(given king) = 4/52 * 4/(1/13)

independent events= when two events dont affect each other. for instance probability of getting 1 then probability of getting 2 will not be affeted by 1

for example: pr(h and t)= pr(h) * pr(t) = 1/2 + 1/2= 1



